01:42:04.590 --> 01:42:06.840
and, you know, that's what I have to defend,

2247
01:42:06.840 --> 01:42:08.400
you know, at all costs.

2248
01:42:08.400 --> 01:42:09.780
And so,

2249
01:42:09.780 --> 01:42:11.100
I wake up

2250
01:42:11.100 --> 01:42:12.690
most days

2251
01:42:12.690 --> 01:42:17.580
and people want me to do something or say something,

2252
01:42:17.580 --> 01:42:20.820
you know, and it's often not in alignment

2253
01:42:20.820 --> 01:42:23.220
with, you know, what I know is right.

2254
01:42:23.220 --> 01:42:25.140
And so, you know,

2255
01:42:25.140 --> 01:42:28.500
not flinching from having those difficult conversations,

2256
01:42:28.500 --> 01:42:31.263
and doing it diplomatically, of course,

2257
01:42:32.220 --> 01:42:35.370
allowing other people to have wins, you know,

2258
01:42:35.370 --> 01:42:36.753
not needing to be right,

2259
01:42:37.620 --> 01:42:39.030
those are some of the things.
I would imagine

2260
01:42:39.030 --> 01:42:40.090
all of those skills

2261
01:42:41.209 --> 01:42:44.220
are enhanced by meditation, right,

2262
01:42:44.220 --> 01:42:47.280
finding that moment of pause,

2263
01:42:47.280 --> 01:42:52.280
where you can process how to best respond versus react,

2264
01:42:52.830 --> 01:42:55.260
how to be tactful in your communication,

2265
01:42:55.260 --> 01:42:56.100
all of those things.

2266
01:42:56.100 --> 01:42:59.790
Do you have a sense of what your leadership was like

2267
01:42:59.790 --> 01:43:02.160
prior to meditation versus now?

2268
01:43:02.160 --> 01:43:06.403
Yes, I was a yeller.
Yeah. (laughs)

2269
01:43:07.500 --> 01:43:09.033
You know, and that's,

2270
01:43:10.800 --> 01:43:14.880
you know, (sighs heavily) I had,

2271
01:43:14.880 --> 01:43:18.090
I had these charms made, and I wore 'em around my neck,

2272
01:43:18.090 --> 01:43:22.143
and one was like two stick figures, like a boy and a girl,

2273
01:43:23.799 --> 01:43:25.950
and had the initials of my kids, E and O,

2274
01:43:25.950 --> 01:43:27.300
and then I had another one made,

2275
01:43:27.300 --> 01:43:31.200
and it said, "Be graceful, yelling doesn't work."

2276
01:43:31.200 --> 01:43:34.440
And that's what I had before I started meditating,

2277
01:43:34.440 --> 01:43:36.393
and I would kind of, you know, rub it,

2278
01:43:37.660 --> 01:43:41.730
and that's what I learned, because it's terrible, you know?

2279
01:43:41.730 --> 01:43:42.563
Yeah.

2280
01:43:44.340 --> 01:43:48.955
And that is, like, I can't ever imagine now yelling.

2281
01:43:48.955 --> 01:43:51.330
I mean, and how horrible, like, to yell,

2282
01:43:51.330 --> 01:43:53.460
like at my kids or, you know,

2283
01:43:53.460 --> 01:43:58.460
at my team or, you know, like a random person, you know?

2284
01:43:58.620 --> 01:44:00.450
I mean, how awful.

2285
01:44:00.450 --> 01:44:03.693
What is the modality of meditation that you practice?

2286
01:44:08.010 --> 01:44:09.420
I do different things.

2287
01:44:09.420 --> 01:44:13.350
Sometimes it's silent, and sometimes it's guided.

2288
01:44:13.350 --> 01:44:15.930
Recently, I've been doing a lot of guided meditations

2289
01:44:15.930 --> 01:44:19.980
because my mind is pretty active.

2290
01:44:19.980 --> 01:44:23.250
At different points, I've been able to do silent meditation,

2291
01:44:23.250 --> 01:44:25.590
but now it's often guided.

2292
01:44:25.590 --> 01:44:26.963
I am a huge fan-
Like on a particular app?

2293
01:44:26.963 --> 01:44:30.210
Yeah, a huge fan of Insight Timer,

2294
01:44:30.210 --> 01:44:33.753
and it keeps track of my days and my minutes and my hours,

2295
01:44:35.249 --> 01:44:37.170
and there are certain practitioners

2296
01:44:37.170 --> 01:44:38.460
on there that I really like.

2297
01:44:38.460 --> 01:44:40.560
I like this woman, Sarah Blondin,

2298
01:44:40.560 --> 01:44:44.670
and there's one particular meditation that she has.

2299
01:44:44.670 --> 01:44:46.080
It's maybe 12 minutes long,

2300
01:44:46.080 --> 01:44:47.970
and it's called "Learning To Surrender",

2301
01:44:47.970 --> 01:44:50.460
and I listened to it on my way here today, you know,

2302
01:44:50.460 --> 01:44:53.130
when it took me longer than I had anticipated,

2303
01:44:53.130 --> 01:44:55.890
and, you know, it's like, I can't be reminded

2304
01:44:55.890 --> 01:44:58.860
too many times to surrender.
Yeah.

2305
01:44:58.860 --> 01:45:00.930
What is the ambition

2306
01:45:00.930 --> 01:45:03.180
for the museum?

2307
01:45:03.180 --> 01:45:04.710
Like, if you have your druthers

2308
01:45:04.710 --> 01:45:07.170
and everything goes your way,

2309
01:45:07.170 --> 01:45:10.650
and it's five years down the road

2310
01:45:10.650 --> 01:45:12.270
and you're looking back,

2311
01:45:12.270 --> 01:45:16.680
what is it that you hope to accomplish or express?

2312
01:45:16.680 --> 01:45:19.320
I want people to feel welcome, you know,

2313
01:45:19.320 --> 01:45:22.260
and it gets back to this idea that I talked about earlier,

2314
01:45:22.260 --> 01:45:25.350
that, you know, like, I know for myself,

2315
01:45:25.350 --> 01:45:28.770
and I use myself as a metric, you know,

2316
01:45:28.770 --> 01:45:31.320
like if I don't care about it, why should I, you know,

2317
01:45:31.320 --> 01:45:33.720
want anyone else to care about it or hope that they will.

2318
01:45:33.720 --> 01:45:36.480
And I know for myself, like,

2319
01:45:36.480 --> 01:45:39.000
what I wanted most in my life, and now,

2320
01:45:39.000 --> 01:45:43.260
which I have so much gratitude that I actually have,

2321
01:45:43.260 --> 01:45:47.100
is, you know, I wanted to feel seen and loved,

2322
01:45:47.100 --> 01:45:50.040
you know, and so much so that I put it in my phone

2323
01:45:50.040 --> 01:45:52.380
and my calendar every morning at 7:00 a.m.,

2324
01:45:52.380 --> 01:45:54.483
and it still buzzes, you know?

2325
01:45:54.483 --> 01:45:57.210
7:00 a.m. Pacific, every morning,

2326
01:45:57.210 --> 01:46:00.510
it says, "I feel seen and loved," and I put it in there,

2327
01:46:00.510 --> 01:46:02.610
and when I put it in, I didn't.

2328
01:46:02.610 --> 01:46:04.760
I didn't feel seen and I didn't feel loved,

2329
01:46:05.610 --> 01:46:08.340
and, you know, I manifested it,

2330
01:46:08.340 --> 01:46:10.740
and so that's what I want.

2331
01:46:10.740 --> 01:46:12.420
That's what I use my platform for,

2332
01:46:12.420 --> 01:46:14.880
and that's what art, for me, is a vehicle for,

2333
01:46:14.880 --> 01:46:17.820
is to have people feel that they're seen

2334
01:46:17.820 --> 01:46:19.380
and feel that they're loved.
Yeah, well,

2335
01:46:19.380 --> 01:46:22.530
I have this sense that all of these many artists

2336
01:46:22.530 --> 01:46:25.620
that you've known and that you chronicle

2337
01:46:25.620 --> 01:46:27.820
in the books and on the podcast

2338
01:46:28.830 --> 01:46:31.950
see you and respect you and revere you.

2339
01:46:31.950 --> 01:46:34.230
I know they think incredibly highly of you,

2340
01:46:34.230 --> 01:46:37.530
and you commandeer, like, a level of respect

2341
01:46:37.530 --> 01:46:41.853
because of that integrity that's so important to you,

2342
01:46:42.750 --> 01:46:44.700
which I think is really cool.

2343
01:46:44.700 --> 01:46:46.770
As you said, like, all you have is your reputation

2344
01:46:46.770 --> 01:46:49.860
and your integrity, and for this creative community

2345
01:46:49.860 --> 01:46:52.260
of, like, brilliant artists all out there,

2346
01:46:52.260 --> 01:46:55.740
who speak so highly of you and think so highly of you,

2347
01:46:55.740 --> 01:46:58.920
it has to be, I mean, that is the fulfillment

2348
01:46:58.920 --> 01:47:01.080
of that 7:00 a.m., like, you know,

2349
01:47:01.080 --> 01:47:03.120
little thing that you get to see every day.

2350
01:47:03.120 --> 01:47:04.623
Yeah, you know.

2351
01:47:06.180 --> 01:47:08.550
You know, I heard this thing some years ago

2352
01:47:08.550 --> 01:47:11.133
about, like, compound interest, you know,

2353
01:47:12.355 --> 01:47:14.310
and it was like about retirement, you know,

2354
01:47:14.310 --> 01:47:16.590
and it's like, if you don't start saving in your 20s,

2355
01:47:16.590 --> 01:47:18.543
like, you can never catch up, right?

2356
01:47:20.400 --> 01:47:23.644
That really stuck with me and, you know,

2357
01:47:23.644 --> 01:47:25.830
I really don't drink, you know,

2358
01:47:27.212 --> 01:47:30.630
I have a mostly vegan, you know, diet.

2359
01:47:30.630 --> 01:47:35.220
You know, I just, I make these kind of hard choices, right,

2360
01:47:35.220 --> 01:47:38.820
and part of it is because,

2361
01:47:38.820 --> 01:47:40.950
like, I'm thinking about the future.

2362
01:47:40.950 --> 01:47:43.260
And so, I'm living in the present,

2363
01:47:43.260 --> 01:47:45.840
but I know that like, all, of these years,

2364
01:47:45.840 --> 01:47:47.110
you know, of meditating

2365
01:47:49.050 --> 01:47:52.080
and, like, standing up for what I believe in

2366
01:47:52.080 --> 01:47:54.330
and defending people's rights

2367
01:47:54.330 --> 01:47:57.240
to show the art that they want to show

2368
01:47:57.240 --> 01:48:02.160
and having the difficult conversations, you know, like,

2369
01:48:02.160 --> 01:48:06.000
that's like in my, like, the bank of my soul.

2370
01:48:06.000 --> 01:48:07.530
Right, yeah, you're making deposits

2371
01:48:07.530 --> 01:48:09.270
in the integrity bank account,

2372
01:48:09.270 --> 01:48:11.700
the karma bank account, right?
Yeah.

2373
01:48:11.700 --> 01:48:14.130
That's been compounding interest all these years.

2374
01:48:14.130 --> 01:48:15.900
Yeah.
Yeah, it's cool.

2375
01:48:15.900 --> 01:48:19.270
Well, the last thing I want to ask you before we wrap it up

2376
01:48:20.760 --> 01:48:23.100
is, you know, it's kind of hearkening back

2377
01:48:23.100 --> 01:48:24.660
to what we were talking about at the beginning

2378
01:48:24.660 --> 01:48:27.030
of the conversation, but just, like,

2379
01:48:27.030 --> 01:48:28.500
for somebody who's listening to this,

2380
01:48:28.500 --> 01:48:31.680
who is still grappling with this idea of, like,

2381
01:48:31.680 --> 01:48:34.170
should I care about this, like I just want to, like,

2382
01:48:34.170 --> 01:48:38.190
leave people with like a little spark of inspiration

2383
01:48:38.190 --> 01:48:41.970
to get them in the door or get them thinking about art

2384
01:48:41.970 --> 01:48:44.310
in a way that maybe historically they haven't.

2385
01:48:44.310 --> 01:48:47.430
Yeah, I mean, what I would say is like,

2386
01:48:47.430 --> 01:48:49.650
what have you got to lose, you know?

2387
01:48:49.650 --> 01:48:52.233
Like, why not try it, you know?

2388
01:48:54.930 --> 01:48:56.940
One of the things we say at the museum is like,

2389
01:48:56.940 --> 01:48:59.190
if you don't like what you see, come back again,

2390
01:48:59.190 --> 01:49:00.750
you know, 'cause it's gonna be different,

2391
01:49:00.750 --> 01:49:01.890
like it's gonna be different,

2392
01:49:01.890 --> 01:49:03.890
and you're gonna be different, you know?

2393
01:49:05.400 --> 01:49:07.020
I did this show in Aspen,

2394
01:49:07.020 --> 01:49:10.620
it was called "Zombies: Pay Attention!",

2395
01:49:10.620 --> 01:49:13.500
and it was inspired by this Bruce Nauman work,

2396
01:49:13.500 --> 01:49:16.080
which is one of my favorite works of art of all time,

2397
01:49:16.080 --> 01:49:18.330
and I may have talked to you about it before,

2398
01:49:19.363 --> 01:49:24.033
but it's writing in reverse, as if it's like in a mirror.

2399
01:49:24.033 --> 01:49:25.108
I don't know if I can swear,

2400
01:49:25.108 --> 01:49:26.580
you know, or not, but it says-
Yeah, you can swear.

2401
01:49:26.580 --> 01:49:28.543
It says, "Pay attention, motherfuckers," you know,

2402
01:49:28.543 --> 01:49:32.160
and, like, that was kind of my mantra for a long time.

2403
01:49:32.160 --> 01:49:35.410
It's like, "Pay attention, motherfuckers," you know,

2404
01:49:35.410 --> 01:49:36.870
like, you only have one life,

2405
01:49:36.870 --> 01:49:38.520
like this moment, (clicks fingers) gone,

2406
01:49:38.520 --> 01:49:39.720
this moment, (clicks fingers) gone,

2407
01:49:39.720 --> 01:49:41.190
this moment, (clicks fingers) gone, you know?

2408
01:49:41.190 --> 01:49:42.870
So, it's like, what do you want to do?

2409
01:49:42.870 --> 01:49:44.730
Like, what are you here to do?

2410
01:49:44.730 --> 01:49:46.327
And Rand Stagen said to me, like,

2411
01:49:46.327 --> 01:49:48.090
"You're doing the world a great disservice

2412
01:49:48.090 --> 01:49:49.350
by playing small."

2413
01:49:49.350 --> 01:49:51.300
So, like, why not look at art?

2414
01:49:51.300 --> 01:49:52.293
Why not try it?

2415
01:49:53.280 --> 01:49:55.140
I think that's a great place to end it.

2416
01:49:55.140 --> 01:49:57.270
That is, I'm inspired now.
(Heidi laughing)

2417
01:49:57.270 --> 01:49:58.103
That worked.

2418
01:50:00.000 --> 01:50:02.220
I love what you do, and I love this person

2419
01:50:02.220 --> 01:50:03.120
that you've become.

2420
01:50:03.120 --> 01:50:07.020
It's been cool to watch you from the sidelines, like,

2421
01:50:07.020 --> 01:50:10.680
mature into this role that you've clearly earned,

2422
01:50:10.680 --> 01:50:13.740
and I just, I salute you, I'm at your service,

2423
01:50:13.740 --> 01:50:14.820
and I think it's great, Heidi.

2424
01:50:14.820 --> 01:50:18.453
So, I appreciate you coming and sharing with me today.

2425
01:50:19.560 --> 01:50:22.680
I wish you well as we near the opening.

2426
01:50:22.680 --> 01:50:24.750
It's gonna be a big moment for you,

2427
01:50:24.750 --> 01:50:26.737
and in the meantime, everybody should pick up

2428
01:50:26.737 --> 01:50:29.190
"Conversations with Artists III".

2429
01:50:29.190 --> 01:50:31.680
Is it still only available

2430
01:50:31.680 --> 01:50:34.897
on the OCMA website?
Yeah, you inspired me,

2431
01:50:34.897 --> 01:50:38.310
you know, with your book, and not having it on Amazon,

2432
01:50:38.310 --> 01:50:43.110
and I was like, why not drive traffic to the OCMA website?

2433
01:50:43.110 --> 01:50:44.250
Yeah.
You know, I mean, honestly,

2434
01:50:44.250 --> 01:50:45.810
the website's not very great yet,

2435
01:50:45.810 --> 01:50:47.730
but it'll get better as we get closer-

2436
01:50:47.730 --> 01:50:50.460
Well, now you have to click Popup to find the book.

2437
01:50:50.460 --> 01:50:51.810
It should at least say "Book"

2438
01:50:51.810 --> 01:50:53.460
or something, you know, to make it

2439
01:50:53.460 --> 01:50:55.271
a little easier for people.
We'll address that, yes.

2440
01:50:55.271 --> 01:50:56.310
(both laughing)

2441
01:50:56.310 --> 01:50:59.377
Yeah, so it's ocma.net?
Art.

2442
01:50:59.377 --> 01:51:01.770
Oh, .art, and then click Popup.

2443
01:51:01.770 --> 01:51:03.810
You'll find the book there.
Yes.

2444
01:51:03.810 --> 01:51:06.810
If you're in Orange County, the museum opens October.

2445
01:51:06.810 --> 01:51:08.460
Do you have a set date?
Yes, we do,

2446
01:51:08.460 --> 01:51:10.560
and I'd actually like to invite everyone

2447
01:51:10.560 --> 01:51:12.570
who's listening to come.
Cool.

2448
01:51:12.570 --> 01:51:16.050
So, October 8th, 5:00 p.m., 24-hour opening.

2449
01:51:16.050 --> 01:51:18.030
So, October 8th, 5:00 p.m.,

2450
01:51:18.030 --> 01:51:19.650
to October 9th, 5:00 p.m.

2451
01:51:19.650 --> 01:51:21.060
Open all night?
Open all night.

2452
01:51:21.060 --> 01:51:23.850
Oh, wow.
Sunrise yoga,

2453
01:51:23.850 --> 01:51:26.610
movies for insomniacs,

2454
01:51:26.610 --> 01:51:31.230
tours of the exhibitions with past curators, directors,

2455
01:51:31.230 --> 01:51:35.413
silent dance party, you know, music, like,

2456
01:51:35.413 --> 01:51:36.892
a ceremony to kick it off.
That sounds pretty cool.

2457
01:51:36.892 --> 01:51:37.860
Something to close.
That sounds like

2458
01:51:37.860 --> 01:51:39.960
a pretty groovy opening.
Yeah.

2459
01:51:39.960 --> 01:51:41.430
Yeah, right on.
It's gonna be amazing,

2460
01:51:41.430 --> 01:51:42.263
and everyone's welcome.

2461
01:51:42.263 --> 01:51:44.250
Awesome.
And totally free.

2462
01:51:44.250 --> 01:51:47.137
Until then, you can also listen to Heidi's podcast,

2463
01:51:47.137 --> 01:51:49.410
"Conversations About Art",

2464
01:51:49.410 --> 01:51:51.390
which you can find on all the podcast platforms.

2465
01:51:51.390 --> 01:51:53.613
Anywhere else you want to direct people?

2466
01:51:54.540 --> 01:51:56.250
I think that's it.
You think that's good?

2467
01:51:56.250 --> 01:51:57.420
Yeah.
All right, how do you feel?

2468
01:51:57.420 --> 01:51:59.040
You feel okay?
I feel great.

2469
01:51:59.040 --> 01:52:00.150
We did it.
Yeah.

2470
01:52:00.150 --> 01:52:02.610
It was cool.
Yeah, I feel like we could,

2471
01:52:02.610 --> 01:52:05.250
you know, do version two and three and four.

2472
01:52:05.250 --> 01:52:06.660
Absolutely, absolutely.
So, yeah,

2473
01:52:06.660 --> 01:52:08.130
lots to talk about.
Yeah, right on.

2474
01:52:08.130 --> 01:52:10.050
All right, I love you, Heidi, thank you.

2475
01:52:10.050 --> 01:52:11.910
To be continued.
Thank you so much.

2476
01:52:11.910 --> 01:52:12.743
Peace.

2477
01:52:12.743 --> 01:52:14.250
